# Read by Docker/Podman from the build context root (repo root) regardless of where the
# Dockerfile itself lives (`infra/docker/Dockerfile`) — see that file's header comment.
# Keep this in sync with `.gitignore`'s intent: exclude anything not needed to build
# `@patches/server`/`@patches/worker` inside the image, and never ship host artifacts that
# get rebuilt in-container anyway (`dist/`, `.turbo/`, `node_modules/`).

# --- dependencies / build output (rebuilt inside the image) ---
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
**/dist/
build/
.turbo/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- vcs / editor / agent ---
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- env / secrets (never bake into an image layer) ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- test / coverage artifacts ---
coverage/
**/coverage/
.nyc_output/

# --- docs (not needed at build time; keeps the context smaller) ---
docs/
*.md
!README.md

# --- local infra not needed inside the image itself ---
infra/compose/
